% ============================================================================
% speleothem-component.query.adj — worked recall over the
% speleothem-component library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to answer "what is a column made
% of?" (direct, TWO answers), "which compound speleothem is a stalagmite
% part of?" (reverse), or "what is a pillar made of?" (abstain — the source
% offers `pillar` as another NAME for a column, not as a second thing, and
% tabling it would double-count one speleothem as two).
%
% It states no fact of its own — it only `import`s the grounded table and
% asks binding queries.
%
% This library exists to CLOSE the `column` abstention that
% `speleothem-growth-surface.adj` recorded. See
% `compound-speleothem-surface.query.adj` for the other half, where the
% surfaces that table declined to bind are recovered by composition.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli speleothem-component.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "speleothem-component.adj"

? speleothem_component(column, $C)          % expect stalactite AND stalagmite -- "they are both, together"
? speleothem_component($Compound, stalagmite) % expect column (reverse)
? speleothem_component(pillar, $C)          % expect abstain -- an alternative NAME for a column, not a second speleothem
? speleothem_component(stalactite, $C)      % expect abstain -- a stalactite is a component, not a compound
? speleothem_component(soda_straw, $C)      % expect abstain -- a developmental STAGE of one speleothem, not two joining
